{
  "raw": {
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Founding-Program-Director--Engineering_R-096845": {
      "title": "Founding Program Director, Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob Title Founding Program Director, Engineering Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Natural & Applied Science Proposed Minimum Salary $8,333.34 monthly Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University–Victoria seeks a full-time, 12-month faculty member for an appointment as a tenure-track Associate or Full Professor or a non-tenure-track Professor of Practice to serve as the Founding Director of the new Bachelor of Science programs in Civil Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, and Software Engineering. The Founding Director will provide leadership for launching, promoting, and advancing these programs and will teach courses within the programs. Qualifications: The Bachelor of Science (BS) degrees in engineering are designed to serve the community in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. The Founding Director will serve as a primary point of contact for Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), with a primary focus on developing and supporting the BS in Civil Engineering, Software Engineering, and Mechanical Engineering with a focus on the intersections between these disciplines. They will also need to satisfy the expectations of Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) and ABET in terms of academic credentials, as well as all other employment qualifications of the University. The programs are anticipated to be open for enrollment Fall 2027. The Founding Director will be employed by A&M-Victoria and will teach face-to-face courses within the University’s academic programs. Victoria is about two hours driving time from Houston, Corpus Christi, Austin, and San Antonio. The Founding Program Director reports to Dean of the College of Natural and Applied Science, working within the Department of Engineering and Aviation Sciences, and has both administrative and instructional responsibilities. The successful candidate should demonstrate the following qualifications: · Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage professional, community, industry, and student audiences. · Ability to plan and implement activities that increase the visibility and profile of the A&M-Victoria Agribusiness concentration within the regional community and agricultural industry. · Demonstrated commitment to supporting and working effectively with students from diverse academic, socioeconomic, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds, as well as students with disabilities. Responsibilities: The individual in this position will be expected to: · Teach classes in service of A&M-Victoria engineering programs, in line with academic credentials and professional experience. Teaching assignments will include face-to-face classes in Victoria, Texas. · Promote A&M-Victoria engineering programs in the greater Victoria region in collaboration with the Division of Enrollment Management. · Direct and oversee the development and equipping of necessary lab and classroom teaching spaces for the proposed engineering degrees. · Be responsible for administrative matters of the department, including teaching, laboratory and research facilities; class rotations and scheduling; budget; and equipment. · Maintain good working relationships with the Independent School Districts and community colleges in Victoria and the surrounding area, as well as with industry partners in the region. · Advise students interested in admission to A&M-Victoria for study in engineering. · Coordinate with the Center for Student Success to ensure that engineering students receive academic advising necessary to foster academic success. · Participate in student activities and campus life and facilitate mentoring for engineering students with industry professionals. · Engage in philanthropic development and community engagement in collaboration with the Office of University Advancement. · Actively participate in affairs of the University, including assisting the engineering programs achieve and maintain ABET program accreditation. · Coordinate with the Career Development Center to develop industry partnerships beneficial to A&M-Victoria and the engineering programs. · Perform other duties as may be necessary and assigned. Because of the University’s outreach mission to serve the broader Texas Gulf Coast region, the position may require travel and occasional work outside of normal business hours. For more information about Texas A&M University-Victoria’s programs and mission, visit www.tamuv.edu. Education and Experience : The position requires an earned master’s degree in engineering or engineering technology. Because this is a professional-track appointment, relevant industry experience in engineering as well as industrial design is expected. An earned doctorate in engineering with prior classroom experience and a knowledge of ABET accreditation and experience leading a program through accreditation is preferred. A current licensure as a professional engineer (mechanical or civil) is strongly preferred. Texas A&M University-Victoria Values : Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the SACSCOC, and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA), and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here. Application: Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position and to apply, visit here. If you have any questions related to the search, please contact Dolores Guerrero (GuerreroD5@tamuv.edu). All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Founding-Program-Director--Aviation_R-096759-2": {
      "title": "Founding Program Director, Aviation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Founding Program Director, Aviation Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Natural & Applied Science Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University–Victoria seeks a full-time, 12-month faculty member for an appointment as a tenure-track Associate or Full Professor or a non-tenure-track Professor of Practice to serve as the Founding Director of the new Bachelor of Science in Aviation program to promote and enhance the degree and teach within the program. Qualifications: Aviation is a new Bachelor of Science (BS) degree designed to serve the community in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. The Founding Director will serve as a primary point of contact for Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), with a primary focus on developing and supporting the BS in Aviation. The Aviation Science Program offers Professional Pilot and Aviation Management pathways. Flight training through a contracted provider will be conducted at the Victoria Regional Airport. The Founding Director will be employed by A&M-Victoria and will teach face-to-face courses within the University’s academic programs. Victoria is about two hours driving time from Houston, Corpus Christi, Austin, and San Antonio. The Victoria region offers great flying weather throughout the year, Class D airspace, a tower-controlled airport, and vast airspace for flight training. The Founding Program Director reports to Dean of the College of Natural and Applied Science, working within the Department of Engineering and Aviation Sciences, and has both administrative and instructional responsibilities, which may include classroom, flight, or ground school instruction. The proportions of each will be negotiated upon hire. The successful candidate should demonstrate the following qualifications: · Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage professional, community, industry, and student audiences. · Ability to plan and implement activities that increase the visibility and profile of the A&M-Victoria Agribusiness concentration within the regional community and agricultural industry. · Demonstrated commitment to supporting and working effectively with students from diverse academic, socioeconomic, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds, as well as students with disabilities. Responsibilities: The individual in this position will be expected to: · Plan and direct all aspects of the aviation program including curriculum development, Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) regulatory compliance, flight operations, scheduling, and accreditation. · Carry out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the College’s policies and applicable laws. · Oversee all operations of the aviation degree program including the flight training contractor. · Oversee all operations of the aviation degree program including the flight training contractor. · Teach courses within the aviation program, including ground school and other subjects as appropriate. Teaching assignments will include face-to-face classes in Victoria, Texas. · Plan and conduct activities that raise the profile of the A&M-Victoria Aviation Science Program within the community and industry. · Actively participate in student recruitment and coordinating with the Division of Enrollment Management to develop recruiting material. · Facilitate mentoring for aviation students with industry professionals and fostering graduate placement. · Identify resource requirements and managing Aviation Program budgets. · Oversee compliance with Aviation Accreditation Board International (AABI) requirements. · Supervise and administer Aviation Program extra-curricular activities and engage with professional organizations, including the National Intercollegiate Flying Association (NIFA). · Perform other duties as may be assigned. Because of the University’s outreach mission to serve the broader Texas Gulf Coast region, the position may require travel and occasional work outside of normal business hours. For more information about Texas A&M University-Victoria’s programs and mission, visit www.tamuv.edu . Education and Experience: The position requires an earned master’s degree in aviation or an equivalent degree or relevant field. Because this is a professional-track appointment, relevant industry experience in aviation and/or flight operations and aviation management is expected (e.g., service as a commercial or military pilot). The position also requires Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) instrument and single-engine land or multi-engine land commercial pilot ratings. Experience as a flight and/or ground school instructor, previous classroom teaching experience in a higher education setting, Single-engine land and multi-engine land pilot ratings, and CFI/Instrument rating is preferred. Texas A&M University-Victoria Values: Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA), and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . Application: Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. If you have any questions related to the search, please contact Dolores Guerrero ( GuerreroD5@tamuv.edu ) All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Tenure-Track-Faculty---Special-Education--ABA-_R-096742-2": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty - Special Education (ABA)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Tenure-Track Faculty - Special Education (ABA) Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Education & Health Professions Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Job Description Texas A&M University-Victoria College of Education and Health Professions is seeking a qualified tenure-track professor to teach graduate special education Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA) classes.  A&M–Victoria is a Hispanic-serving institution, located in the Coastal Bend region of southeast Texas. The campus is in Victoria, TX, approximately 2 hours from Houston, Austin, Corpus Christi, and San Antonio. A&M–Victoria enrolls approximately 3,300 students.  This position is based in Victoria, TX. The successful applicant is expected to play a role in supporting graduate teaching, thus contributing to campus and student life in Victoria. Our Special Education department offers an M.Ed in Special Education Applied Behavior Analysis to prepare students to become credentialed behavior analysts.   The position requires the Clinical Professor to teach courses each fall and spring semester, advise students and oversee the program including taking steps toward accreditation.  Position summary:  The position is based in Victoria, Texas.   It is a nine-month clinical track position. The sum of responsibilities include teaching graduate classes; overseeing the SPED ABA program including program and curriculum development toward accreditation; collecting data for program review and advising students. Candidates are expected to maintain excellence in teaching; participate in course and program development; perform other duties as assigned by the Dean of the College of Education and Health Professions and the Chair of the Department of Educational Leadership, Postsecondary Education, and Special Education, and perform all other related activities as required. This position will start in Fall 2026 and is renewable on an annual basis. Opportunities for summer teaching might be available based on demand and departmental need. Required Qualifications: Doctorate in Applied Behavior Analysis, Special Education or Educational Psychology    Experience in special education in K-12 public schools working with students with disabilities Experience teaching online BCBA-D credential Ability to guide students in experimental research for capstone projects For questions about the position, please contact Mary Lasater ( LasaterM@tamuv.edu ) Applicants must apply online and include: * A cover letter * A current curriculum vitae *A list of three professional references who are in a position to know the applicant’s expertise, with at least two addressing teaching effectiveness; letters of recommendation will be requested during the final stages of the search. * Evidence of effective teaching, such a statement of teaching philosophy or student evaluations, if available *Copies of all college transcripts (official transcripts will be required of all finalists)  Salary is competitive. Review of applications will begin on September 17, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A Closer Look at A&M-Victoria Texas A&M University-Victoria is a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world and is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. A&M-Victoria promotes economic development and advances the quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, we are driven by a relentless pursuit of excellence. As a next-generation university, we redefine the boundaries of higher education, creating opportunities for students from all backgrounds to excel. Our unwavering focus on student success and research innovation sets us apart, positioning A&M-Victoria as a model for universities of the future. Texas A&M University-Victoria Values : Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Our History Since our establishment in 1973, we have grown into a vibrant institution with a reputation for academic excellence and a dedication to student success. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, our history is a testament to our commitment to providing quality education and fostering academic achievement. Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System – making it the 12th campus in the System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. City Location A regional hub 30 miles inland from the Gulf of Mexico, Victoria is a town of 65,000 located about two hours from Houston, Austin, San Antonio and Corpus Christi. Located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas, A&M-Victoria serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Mission Statement  Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world, is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. Texas A&M University-Victoria promotes economic development and advances quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Our Goals Continually enhance the quality of our student experience. Promote and expand access to education. Increase community engagements and increase public events for diverse audiences on our campuses. Promote a culture of institutional identification among stakeholders Academic Excellence Several of A&M-Victoria’s academic degree programs have drawn top rankings from organizations including College Consensus, Intelligent.com and Research.com. Our Accreditations include: SACSCOC Accredited, AACSB Accredited, ABET Accredited, CACREP Accredited, NASP Accredited, and TASP Accredited The Texas A&M University System is one of the largest and most impactful higher education systems in the country, with an annual budget of $7.3 billion. Its statewide network includes 12 universities, a comprehensive health science center, eight state agencies, Texas A&M–Fort Worth and the Texas A&M–RELLIS. The System serves nearly 180,000 students and reaches millions more through service, research and outreach programs each year. With nearly $1.6 billion in annual research expenditures, the System fuels innovation, supports communities and drives Texas’ economy forward. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Founding-Program-Director--Bachelor-of-Business-Administration---Agribusiness_R-096816": {
      "title": "Founding Program Director, Bachelor of Business Administration - Agribusiness",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Founding Program Director, Bachelor of Business Administration - Agribusiness Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Business Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University–Victoria seeks a full-time, 12-month faculty member for an appointment as a tenure-track Associate or Full Professor or a non-tenure-track Professor of Practice to serve as the Founding Director of the BBA, Agribusiness program to promote and enhance the Agribusiness concentration and teach within the program. Qualifications: Agribusiness is a new concentration within the Bachelor of Business Administration (BBA) degree designed to serve the agricultural community in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. The Founding Director will serve as a primary point of contact for Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), with a primary focus on developing and supporting the BBA concentration in Agribusiness. The Founding Director will be employed by A&M-Victoria and will teach face-to-face courses within the University’s academic programs. Accordingly, the successful candidate must meet the academic credentialing requirements of Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) and AACSB, as well as all other employment qualifications established by the University. The successful candidate should demonstrate the following qualifications: · Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage professional, community, industry, and student audiences. · Ability to plan and implement activities that increase the visibility and profile of the A&M-Victoria Agribusiness concentration within the regional community and agricultural industry. · Demonstrated commitment to supporting and working effectively with students from diverse academic, socioeconomic, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds, as well as students with disabilities. Responsibilities: The individual in this position will be expected to: · Teach multiple courses each semester, primarily at the undergraduate level, through face-to-face instruction in Victoria, Texas. · Provide leadership for the recruitment, growth, and ongoing development of the Agribusiness concentration, including course and curriculum development. · Respond effectively and sensitively to the educational needs of a diverse population of current and prospective students. · Engage in university and professional service and collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, industry partners, community organizations, and other stakeholders. · Perform other duties as assigned by the dean and department chair. Because of the University’s outreach mission to serve the broader Texas Gulf Coast region, the position may require travel and occasional work outside of normal business hours. For more information about Texas A&M University-Victoria’s programs and mission, visit www.tamuv.edu. Education and Experience: The position requires an earned master’s degree in business or agribusiness. Because this is a professional-track appointment, relevant industry experience in agribusiness is expected. An earned doctorate in business or agribusiness and prior teaching experience in higher education are preferred. Texas A&M University-Victoria Values: Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the SACSCOC, and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA), and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . Application: Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. If you have any questions related to the search, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Yixi Ning (NingY@TAMUV.edu). All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Exec-Admin-Asst-to-VP-Enrl-Mgm_R-096644": {
      "title": "Exec Admin Asst to VP Enrl Mgm",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Exec Admin Asst to VP Enrl Mgm Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department Enrollment Management Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The Executive Administrative Assistant to the Vice President for Enrollment Management, under general supervision, provides high-level administrative, operational, and executive support to the Vice President and the Enrollment Management division. Work involves coordinating the administrative operations of the division, supporting executive priorities and initiatives, and serving as a key resource and liaison for departments within Enrollment Management. Exercises discretion, independent judgment, initiative, and sound judgment with respect to matters of significance and serves as a strategic administrative partner to the division. Responsibilities: Coordinates complex calendars, meetings, appointments, travel, and other activities for the Vice President and Enrollment Management. Proactively identifies and resolves scheduling conflicts and coordinates competing priorities to maximize efficiency. Provides administrative guidance and support to the Vice President, directors, managers, and staff within Enrollment Management. Coordinates and monitors action items, assignments, deadlines, and deliverables and provides follow-up and status updates. Drafts and manages executive correspondence, communications, reports, presentations, agendas, briefing materials, talking points, and other documents. Coordinates communication and follow-up with internal and external stakeholders on behalf of the Vice President and division. Assists with compiling reports, researching and evaluating information, maintaining records and documentation, and preparing materials to support executive decision-making, divisional planning, and operational activities. Supports HR-related administrative functions for Enrollment Management, including recruitment and hiring processes, employee documentation, onboarding, personnel actions, Workday tasks, and coordination with Human Resources. Assists with divisional budget and fiscal activities, including purchasing, invoices, expense tracking, budget documentation, financial records, and related administrative processes. Coordinates with appropriate university offices to facilitate timely and accurate financial transactions. Communicates and assists with interpreting university and divisional policies, procedures, standards, and administrative requirements. Responds to inquiries, resolves routine administrative matters, and appropriately escalates sensitive or complex issues. Anticipates executive and divisional needs, identifies potential scheduling, administrative, or operational concerns, and recommends solutions or process improvements before they affect divisional operations. Plans and coordinates logistical and administrative support for meetings, events, conferences, special functions, and Enrollment Management initiatives. Provides on-site support and coordinates necessary resources, materials, and arrangements. Coordinates travel arrangements, registrations, itineraries, and related documentation for the Vice President and designated staff. May prepare, review, and process travel reimbursements in accordance with university policies. Maintains organized, accurate, and confidential records, files, correspondence, and documentation to support institutional continuity, accountability, compliance, and effective divisional operations. Develops and maintains a working knowledge of Enrollment Management departments, programs, processes, systems, organizational structures, and priorities to effectively anticipate needs and support executive decision-making and operational execution. Serves as a central administrative liaison and resource for Enrollment Management departments, coordinating departmental requests, special projects, university initiatives, and cross-functional activities to promote communication and collaboration throughout the division. Monitors divisional priorities, action items, deadlines, and outstanding deliverables and provides leadership with timely updates regarding progress, follow-up needs, and potential concerns. Exercises sound judgment, discretion, professionalism, and confidentiality when handling sensitive executive, personnel, financial, student, and institutional information. Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Three years of related experience. Experience supporting executive leadership or senior-level administrators preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of administrative practices, procedures, and organizational operations. Knowledge of HR administrative processes, budgeting, purchasing, financial documentation, and general office operations preferred. Knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet, presentation, calendar, and other office productivity applications. Ability to manage multiple priorities, competing deadlines, and complex administrative responsibilities. Ability to exercise independent judgment, discretion, initiative, and sound decision-making. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Strong planning, organizational, problem-solving, and project coordination skills. Ability to anticipate needs, resolve issues, and work proactively with limited direction. Ability to research, compile, evaluate, and communicate information effectively. Ability to maintain confidentiality and establish effective working relationships with executives, administrators, faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders. Ability to adapt to changing priorities and work effectively in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. Starting salary for this position is $3,657.33 monthly and is negotiable depending on education and experience. A Closer Look at A&M-Victoria Texas A&M University-Victoria is a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world and is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. A&M-Victoria promotes economic development and advances the quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, we are driven by a relentless pursuit of excellence. As a next-generation university, we redefine the boundaries of higher education, creating opportunities for students from all backgrounds to excel. Our unwavering focus on student success and research innovation sets us apart, positioning A&M-Victoria as a model for universities of the future. Our History Since our establishment in 1973, we have grown into a vibrant institution with a reputation for academic excellence and a dedication to student success. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, our history is a testament to our commitment to providing quality education and fostering academic achievement. Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System – making it the 12th campus in the System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. City Location A regional hub 30 miles inland from the Gulf of Mexico, Victoria is a town of 65,000 located about two hours from Houston, Austin, San Antonio and Corpus Christi. Located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas, A&M-Victoria serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Mission Statement  Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world, is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. Texas A&M University-Victoria promotes economic development and advances quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Our Goals Continually enhance the quality of our student experience. Promote and expand access to education. Increase community engagements and increase public events for diverse audiences on our campuses. Promote a culture of institutional identification among stakeholders Academic Excellence Several of A&M-Victoria’s academic degree programs have drawn top rankings from organizations including College Consensus, Intelligent.com and Research.com. Our Accreditations include: SACSCOC Accredited, AACSB Accredited, ABET Accredited, CACREP Accredited, NASP Accredited, and TASP Accredited The Texas A&M University System is one of the largest and most impactful higher education systems in the country, with an annual budget of $7.3 billion. Its statewide network includes 12 universities, a comprehensive health science center, eight state agencies, Texas A&M–Fort Worth and the Texas A&M–RELLIS. The System serves nearly 180,000 students and reaches millions more through service, research and outreach programs each year. With nearly $1.6 billion in annual research expenditures, the System fuels innovation, supports communities and drives Texas’ economy forward. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Assistant-Director--Human-Resources_R-096782": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Human Resources",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Director, Human Resources Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department Human Resources Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The Assistant Director, Human Resources, under direction, organizes, manages, and leads human resource functions. Develops schedules, priorities, and standards for achieving goals. Provides guidance to departments and management regarding HR practices, compliance, laws, regulations, and ethics. Researches and completes various projects, as requested by the HR Leadership. Responsibilities: -Organizes, manages, and leads human resources unit. Develops schedules, priorities, and standards for achieving goals. -Assists in developing strategic plans for the human resources unit. -Provides guidance to departments and management regarding HR practices, compliance, laws, regulations, and ethics. Effectively communicates HR programs, practices, and policies to employees. Ensures compliance with state and federal laws and regulations. Effectively communicates with HR leaders. -Oversees and/or prepares reports and documents related to human resources activities. -Oversees and manages the specialized training program. Oversees the development and revisions made to training materials. -Oversees and approves actions in the HRIS System or related systems. Resolves and troubleshoots escalated and complex issues. -Advises management on the administration of operating plans and policies for human resource activities. -Develops and revises guidelines, policies, regulations, rules, and standard administrative procedures. audits of human resources to ensure compliance with policies and procedures. -Advises staff and management on issues, rules, policies, regulations, and standard administrative procedures related to human resources management. -Researches and completes various projects, as requested by the HR Leadership. -Partners with managers to understand the department’s current and future HR challenges, and identify HR needs and opportunities for improvement. -Develops formal and informal messages as appropriate for intended audiences. -As needed, works with international services, faculty affairs, student employment, graduate professional school, research, payroll, and tax on highly complex questions and requests. -Develops and maintains network of professional contacts within the university including peers in HR and non-HR roles, customers, and management. -May oversee and manage specialized HR events and programs. -May serve as a back up in another specialized human resource function in an assigned area, such as benefits, classification and compensation, employee relations, immigration, leave, onboarding, payroll, performance evaluation/management, organization development, recognition/rewards, recruitment, and workers’ compensation. -Attends human resources trainings and/or informational meetings. -Recruits, hires, trains, supervises, evaluates performance, and develops professional development plans for assigned staff.   Education and Experience: -Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources Management, Business Administration, or applicable field, or equivalent combination of education and experience. -Five years of related experience. Required Attachments: Resume, Cover Letter Texas A&M University-Victoria Values: Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA), and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Director--Career-Development-Center_R-096729": {
      "title": "Director, Career Development Center",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Director, Career Development Center Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department Provost Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Texas A&M University-Victoria seeks a full-time, 12-month Director of the Career Development Center to lead career development and student employment services. Qualifications: The Director will connect academic programs and student experiences with career counseling, professional development, internships, employment, and graduate opportunities from enrollment through graduation and beyond. Under the direction and supervision of the Executive Director of Student Success, this position will oversee career programming, employer engagement, job development and potential placement, student employment, and career resources while managing departmental budgets and supporting student and alumni career success. Prior experience advising college students and familiarity with programs like Handshake, EAB Navigate, and Slate are desirable. Responsibilities: · Lead career development services that integrate academic programs, career counseling, experiential learning, and employment preparation from freshman year through graduation and throughout students’ evolving careers. · Partner with academic deans, chairs, and faculty to align career pathways, internships, and professional development with academic programs and workforce needs. · Provide career counseling and assessment to help students and alumni explore careers, identify goals, develop professional skills, and plan for employment or graduate education. · Develop progressive career-readiness programming that supports students from early career exploration as freshmen, through skill and experience development as sophomores and juniors, to job/graduate school preparation and potential placement as seniors. · Build internships, experiential learning, employer partnerships, and networking opportunities that connect classroom learning to careers. · Provide workshops and individualized coaching in resumes, interviewing, job searching, networking, and other professional skills. · Cultivate and maintain relationships with employers and leverage campuswide networks and relationships to grow employer partners. · Coordinate career fairs, employer recruitment, on-campus interviewing, student employment, and job placement activities. · Assess career programs and use outcome data to strengthen services and student employment success. · Supervise staff and manage related programs, resources, and partnerships. Texas A&M University-Victoria Values: Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree required, Master’s preferred in Counseling, Business, Higher Education, or related area and six years of related experience. Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA), and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . Application: Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. Starting salary for this position is $5,000 monthly and is negotiable depending on education and experience. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Dir-International-Programs_R-096608": {
      "title": "Dir,International Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Dir,International Programs Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department International Programs Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The Director of International Programs leads the development and administration of the university’s international education portfolio, including global partnerships, study abroad and exchange programs, and initiatives that support international student engagement. The position works across academic and administrative areas to establish and strengthen international collaborations, develop new global opportunities, and ensure programs meet institutional goals and applicable requirements. Responsibilities include overseeing program operations and budgets, supervising staff, coordinating student support and risk management, evaluating program outcomes, and representing the university with international partners and organizations. The Director also serves as a key resource to faculty, academic departments, and university leadership on international program development and global engagement. Education and Experience: -Bachelor’s degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. -Ten years of related experience. Required attachments : Resume and cover letter Starting salary for this position is $5,192.41 monthly and is negotiable depending on education and experience. A Closer Look at A&M-Victoria Texas A&M University-Victoria is a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world and is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. A&M-Victoria promotes economic development and advances the quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, we are driven by a relentless pursuit of excellence. As a next-generation university, we redefine the boundaries of higher education, creating opportunities for students from all backgrounds to excel. Our unwavering focus on student success and research innovation sets us apart, positioning A&M-Victoria as a model for universities of the future. Our History Since our establishment in 1973, we have grown into a vibrant institution with a reputation for academic excellence and a dedication to student success. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, our history is a testament to our commitment to providing quality education and fostering academic achievement. Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System – making it the 12th campus in the System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. City Location A regional hub 30 miles inland from the Gulf of Mexico, Victoria is a town of 65,000 located about two hours from Houston, Austin, San Antonio and Corpus Christi. Located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas, A&M-Victoria serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Mission Statement  Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world, is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. Texas A&M University-Victoria promotes economic development and advances quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Our Goals Continually enhance the quality of our student experience. Promote and expand access to education. Increase community engagements and increase public events for diverse audiences on our campuses. Promote a culture of institutional identification among stakeholders Academic Excellence Several of A&M-Victoria’s academic degree programs have drawn top rankings from organizations including College Consensus, Intelligent.com and Research.com. Our Accreditations include: SACSCOC Accredited, AACSB Accredited, ABET Accredited, CACREP Accredited, NASP Accredited, and TASP Accredited The Texas A&M University System is one of the largest and most impactful higher education systems in the country, with an annual budget of $7.3 billion. Its statewide network includes 12 universities, a comprehensive health science center, eight state agencies, Texas A&M–Fort Worth and the Texas A&M–RELLIS. The System serves nearly 180,000 students and reaches millions more through service, research and outreach programs each year. With nearly $1.6 billion in annual research expenditures, the System fuels innovation, supports communities and drives Texas’ economy forward. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Assistant-Director-of-Environmental-Health---Safety_R-096475": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Environmental Health & Safety",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Director of Environmental Health & Safety Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department Emergency Management Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Under general direction, the Assistant Director of Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) leads, plans, and administers campus EHS programs to support a safe and healthy environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors at Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria). The position establishes, implements, and maintains programs in industrial hygiene, laboratory safety, occupational safety, environmental compliance, hazardous materials management, emergency spill response, and other environmental health and safety disciplines, as appropriate. This position is responsible for ensuring that EHS programs are administered in accordance with applicable state, federal, and Texas A&M University System (A&M System) guidelines and regulations. Responsibilities 1. Program Leadership and Compliance · Leads the planning, implementation, and evaluation of EHS programs that promote a safe and healthy environment for faculty, staff, students, and visitors. · Establishes and maintains programs in industrial hygiene, laboratory safety, occupational safety, emergency response, environmental compliance, and hazardous materials management, as appropriate. · Ensures compliance and alignment with applicable local, state, federal, university, and A&M System policies, regulations, and industry best practices. · Evaluates the impact of new or revised regulations on operations, services, and programs and communicates relevant changes to the university community, as appropriate. 2. Operational Oversight · Oversees hazardous waste management, campus chemical inventory, hazardous materials shipping, Tier II reporting, and related chemical and environmental compliance activities. · Directs chemical safety and laboratory safety programs, including chemical hygiene practices, hazard communication, safe chemical storage, handling and use, laboratory inspections, risk assessments, and follow-up actions. · Provides industrial hygiene assessments, indoor air quality assessments, exposure evaluations, and related workplace health hazard assessment activities, as appropriate. · Reviews and approves construction and renovation project plans and monitors recommended changes to support compliance with applicable environmental health and laboratory safety requirements and best practices. · Supports incident and emergency spill response activities and implements improvements based on lessons learned, risk trends, and operational needs. · Evaluates the effectiveness of departmental operations and recommends organizational or programmatic changes needed to maintain effective and compliant EHS programs. 3. Leadership, Representation, and Administration · Supervises, trains, and develops staff and maintains a qualified workforce to support departmental operations. · Represents EHS to university leadership, committees, regulatory agencies, external partners, and the public, and serves as the university’s primary liaison with local, state, and federal regulatory agencies. · Develops departmental budgets, monitors expenditures, and prepares or oversees routine and special reports on departmental operations, costs, and programs. · Provides training, communication, and subject-matter guidance to faculty, staff, students, and other stakeholders to support awareness and compliance. Qualifications: Required Education & Experienc e · Bachelor’s degree in an applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. · Sixteen years of experience in environmental health and safety, including two years of supervisory experience. Required Competencies · Ability to maintain the security and integrity of critical infrastructure, which may include communications systems, computer networks, cybersecurity systems, the electrical grid, hazardous waste treatment systems, and water treatment systems. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities · Knowledge of TCEQ, TDSHS, and NFPA regulations. · Proficiency with Microsoft Office and safety equipment appropriate to areas of responsibility. · Excellent written and oral communication skills. · Experience interacting with local, state, and federal regulatory agencies. Preferred Qualifications · Five years of progressively responsible management experience in a higher education safety organization. · Licensed by the Texas Department of State Health Services as: · Asbestos Management Planner · Asbestos Inspector o Mold Assessment Consultant · Sanitarian · Master’s degree in industrial hygiene, environmental management, safety, or related field. · Certifications by nationally recognized safety organizations (e.g., radiation safety, fire safety, industrial hygiene, occupational safety, hazardous materials). Additional Information · This position is designated as essential personnel and will require participation in emergency response and after-hours operations. · The position may require occasional travel to coordinate with System Offices, agencies, and external partners. Required Attachments : Resume, Cover Letter, References   Starting salary for this position is $7,651.00 monthly and is negotiable depending on education and experience. A Closer Look at A&M-Victoria Texas A&M University-Victoria is a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world and is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. A&M-Victoria promotes economic development and advances the quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, we are driven by a relentless pursuit of excellence. As a next-generation university, we redefine the boundaries of higher education, creating opportunities for students from all backgrounds to excel. Our unwavering focus on student success and research innovation sets us apart, positioning A&M-Victoria as a model for universities of the future. Our History Since our establishment in 1973, we have grown into a vibrant institution with a reputation for academic excellence and a dedication to student success. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, our history is a testament to our commitment to providing quality education and fostering academic achievement. Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System – making it the 12th campus in the System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. City Location A regional hub 30 miles inland from the Gulf of Mexico, Victoria is a town of 65,000 located about two hours from Houston, Austin, San Antonio and Corpus Christi. Located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas, A&M-Victoria serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Mission Statement  Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world, is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. Texas A&M University-Victoria promotes economic development and advances quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Our Goals Continually enhance the quality of our student experience. Promote and expand access to education. Increase community engagements and increase public events for diverse audiences on our campuses. Promote a culture of institutional identification among stakeholders Academic Excellence Several of A&M-Victoria’s academic degree programs have drawn top rankings from organizations including College Consensus, Intelligent.com and Research.com. Our Accreditations include: SACSCOC Accredited, AACSB Accredited, ABET Accredited, CACREP Accredited, NASP Accredited, and TASP Accredited The Texas A&M University System is one of the largest and most impactful higher education systems in the country, with an annual budget of $7.3 billion. Its statewide network includes 12 universities, a comprehensive health science center, eight state agencies, Texas A&M–Fort Worth and the Texas A&M–RELLIS. The System serves nearly 180,000 students and reaches millions more through service, research and outreach programs each year. With nearly $1.6 billion in annual research expenditures, the System fuels innovation, supports communities and drives Texas’ economy forward. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Director--Fire-and-Life-Safety_R-096474": {
      "title": "Director, Fire and Life Safety",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Director, Fire and Life Safety Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department Emergency Management Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Under general direction, the Director, Fire and Life Safety serves as the senior campus official responsible for all fire and life safety, emergency management, and incident preparedness activities at Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria). This position is responsible for the development and oversight of essential campus functions such as fire prevention, inspection, plan review, code enforcement, emergency operations, and continuity planning The Fire Marshal & Director of Emergency Management ensures a safe learning and working environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors through proactive program development, regulatory compliance, emergency response leadership, and collaborative engagement across all campus units. Responsibilities: 40% – Fire & Life Safety Leadership and Program Administration · Serves as the Campus Fire Marshal, or the Local Authority Having Jurisdiction (Local AHJ) for fire and life safety and is responsible for all aspects of the fire and life safety program. · Directs all fire prevention, inspection, and code enforcement programs, including plan review, system testing oversight, and building fire safety compliance. · Reviews and approves construction and renovation plans for fire and life safety requirements; ensures integration of NFPA and ICC codes. · Oversees fire protection systems, hot work procedures, event permitting, special occupancy reviews, and life safety risk assessments. · Ensures campus compliance with current codes adopted by the Texas State Fire Marshal’s Office (SFMO) and A&M System Regulation 34.01.02 Fire and Life Safety. · Develops and delivers fire and life safety education, training, and outreach for the campus community. · Facilitates or ensures appropriate completion of fire investigations, cause/origin assessments, and associated reporting. · Serves as the primary liaison with local fire departments, building officials, and other regulatory agencies. 35% – Emergency Management Leadership · Directs A&M-Victoria’s Emergency Management Program, ensuring compliance with System Policy 34.07 Emergency Management, and System Regulations 34.07.01 Emergency Operations Plans, and 34.07.02 Business Continuity Plans. · Develops, maintains, and updates the A&M-Victoria Emergency Operations Plan (EOP), hazard-specific annexes, incident response guides, and continuity plans. · Coordinates the campus Emergency Operations Center (EOC) and leads all campus preparedness, mitigation, response, and recovery efforts. · Designs and conducts emergency exercises, drills, tabletops, and full-scale events; completes After-Action Reviews and manages corrective action plans. · Oversees emergency preparedness education, outreach, and campus-wide training. · Coordinates emergency planning and response with city, county, state, and federal partners. · Responds to on-campus emergencies, special events, and after-hours incidents as required. 15% – Programmatic Support, Compliance & Administrative Oversight · Develop procedures, standards, and protocols supporting comprehensive Fire and Life Safety and Emergency Management programs. · Maintains operational documents, records, compliance reporting, and regulatory correspondence. · Supports campus risk reduction initiatives, hazard mitigation planning, and safety culture development. 10% – Staff Supervision, Representation & Campus Engagement · Supervises personnel supporting fire safety, emergency management, inspections, equipment maintenance, or code compliance. · Represents A&M-Victoria on local, regional, and system-wide fire safety and emergency management committees. · Serves as the institution’s primary interface with regulatory agency officials for fire safety and emergency management-related matters. · Provides guidance to campus leadership on campus life safety requirements, compliance risks, and emergency readiness strategies. Qualifications: Required Education & Experience · Bachelor’s degree in an applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. · Twelve years of combined experience in fire and life safety, emergency management, environmental health and safety, or a closely related field. Required Licenses & Certifications · NFPA Fire Inspector I. · Fire Inspector and Plans Examiner certifications (TCFP, ICC, or NFPA). Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities · Comprehensive knowledge of NFPA, ICC, TCEQ, and TDSHS regulations. · Ability to interpret and apply fire and life safety codes in complex or non-standard environments. · Strong leadership, supervisory, and communication skills. · Ability to collaborate effectively with diverse stakeholders and regulatory agencies. · Proficiency with Microsoft Office and safety-related software and equipment. · Completion of FEMA/NIMS (IS-100, 200, 300, 400, 700, 800). Preferred Qualifications · Five (5) years in an increasingly responsible management position in a higher education safety organization. · Master’s degree in emergency management, public administration, safety, or related field. · Fire Investigator, Fire & Life Safety Educator, or additional ICC/NFPA/TCFP certifications. · Associate Emergency Manager (AEM) or Certified Emergency Manager (CEM) certification · FEMA Professional or Master Continuity Practitioner Additional Information · This position is designated as essential personnel and will require participation in emergency response and after-hours operations. · The position may require occasional travel to coordinate with System Offices, agencies, and external partners. Required Attachments : Resume, Cover Letter, References A Closer Look at A&M-Victoria Texas A&M University-Victoria is a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world and is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. A&M-Victoria promotes economic development and advances the quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, we are driven by a relentless pursuit of excellence. As a next-generation university, we redefine the boundaries of higher education, creating opportunities for students from all backgrounds to excel. Our unwavering focus on student success and research innovation sets us apart, positioning A&M-Victoria as a model for universities of the future. Our History Since our establishment in 1973, we have grown into a vibrant institution with a reputation for academic excellence and a dedication to student success. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, our history is a testament to our commitment to providing quality education and fostering academic achievement. Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System – making it the 12th campus in the System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. City Location A regional hub 30 miles inland from the Gulf of Mexico, Victoria is a town of 65,000 located about two hours from Houston, Austin, San Antonio and Corpus Christi. Located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas, A&M-Victoria serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Mission Statement  Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world, is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. Texas A&M University-Victoria promotes economic development and advances quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Our Goals Continually enhance the quality of our student experience. Promote and expand access to education. Increase community engagements and increase public events for diverse audiences on our campuses. Promote a culture of institutional identification among stakeholders Academic Excellence Several of A&M-Victoria’s academic degree programs have drawn top rankings from organizations including College Consensus, Intelligent.com and Research.com. Our Accreditations include: SACSCOC Accredited, AACSB Accredited, ABET Accredited, CACREP Accredited, NASP Accredited, and TASP Accredited The Texas A&M University System is one of the largest and most impactful higher education systems in the country, with an annual budget of $7.3 billion. Its statewide network includes 12 universities, a comprehensive health science center, eight state agencies, Texas A&M–Fort Worth and the Texas A&M–RELLIS. The System serves nearly 180,000 students and reaches millions more through service, research and outreach programs each year. With nearly $1.6 billion in annual research expenditures, the System fuels innovation, supports communities and drives Texas’ economy forward. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Budget-Specialist-I_R-096434": {
      "title": "Budget Specialist I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Budget Specialist I Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department Budget Office Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The Budget Specialist I, under supervision, performs routine budget preparation and analysis work. Responsibilities: -Prepares journal and budget entries. Collects, analyzes, and reports data -Provides advice and assistance concerning budget and funding procedures and methods -Assists in the monitoring, processing and tracking requests -Assists in reviewing, evaluating, and preparing request for funds -Assists in the preparation of annual operating budget -Assists in the preparation of legislative appropriations requests, fiscal notes, and analysis of legislation -Conducts training Education and Experience: -Bachelor’s degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: -Knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet, and database applications. -Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Required Attachments : Resume, Cover Letter   Starting salary for this position is $3333.34 monthly and is negotiable depending on education and experience. A Closer Look at A&M-Victoria Texas A&M University-Victoria is a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world and is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. A&M-Victoria promotes economic development and advances the quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, we are driven by a relentless pursuit of excellence. As a next-generation university, we redefine the boundaries of higher education, creating opportunities for students from all backgrounds to excel. Our unwavering focus on student success and research innovation sets us apart, positioning A&M-Victoria as a model for universities of the future. Our History Since our establishment in 1973, we have grown into a vibrant institution with a reputation for academic excellence and a dedication to student success. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, our history is a testament to our commitment to providing quality education and fostering academic achievement. Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System – making it the 12th campus in the System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. City Location A regional hub 30 miles inland from the Gulf of Mexico, Victoria is a town of 65,000 located about two hours from Houston, Austin, San Antonio and Corpus Christi. Located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas, A&M-Victoria serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Mission Statement  Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world, is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. Texas A&M University-Victoria promotes economic development and advances quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Our Goals Continually enhance the quality of our student experience. Promote and expand access to education. Increase community engagements and increase public events for diverse audiences on our campuses. Promote a culture of institutional identification among stakeholders Academic Excellence Several of A&M-Victoria’s academic degree programs have drawn top rankings from organizations including College Consensus, Intelligent.com and Research.com. Our Accreditations include: SACSCOC Accredited, AACSB Accredited, ABET Accredited, CACREP Accredited, NASP Accredited, and TASP Accredited The Texas A&M University System is one of the largest and most impactful higher education systems in the country, with an annual budget of $7.3 billion. Its statewide network includes 12 universities, a comprehensive health science center, eight state agencies, Texas A&M–Fort Worth and the Texas A&M–RELLIS. The System serves nearly 180,000 students and reaches millions more through service, research and outreach programs each year. With nearly $1.6 billion in annual research expenditures, the System fuels innovation, supports communities and drives Texas’ economy forward. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
